dmenu - dynamic menu
====================
dmenu is an efficient dynamic menu for X.


Requirements
------------
In order to build dmenu you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (dmenu is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install dmenu
(if necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running dmenu
-------------
See the man page for details.


Optional title and preview
--------------------------
A title appears above the search field when -title is specified. The existing
compact menu layout remains unchanged without a title or preview.

Example with a live Wi-Fi information provider:

    wifi_list | dmenu -i -c -l 10 -p Search \
        -title 'Wi-Fi Networks' \
        -preview wifi_info -preview-title 'Network details' \
        -preview-pos right -preview-size 45

The optional preview adds a right-hand text panel on vertical menus. Each time
the highlighted row changes, dmenu executes the named executable directly
with the selected item as its sole argument and in DMENU_ITEM. It does not
invoke a shell or substitute user-controlled text into a command string.
The executable must be discoverable in PATH (or be an absolute pathname).
To pass custom arguments, create a wrapper script with a fixed interface.

Preview commands run asynchronously, with a 3-second time limit and an 8 KiB
output limit. A superseded preview is cancelled; the menu remains responsive.
The preview is text-only, with no image or external GUI toolkit dependency.
The preview-size setting is the percentage of menu width, from 20 to 70.
Only -preview-pos right is currently supported. Preview content is ignored
on horizontal menus; use -l for vertical menus.

Test supported flags before launching X11:

    sh tests/cli-options.sh

After rebuilding, test interactively under X11:

    make clean && make
    printf 'One\nTwo\n' | ./dmenu -c -l 2 -title 'Test' -p 'Search'
    printf 'One\nTwo\n' | ./dmenu -c -l 2 -title 'Test' \
        -preview /usr/bin/printf -preview-title 'Details'

No existing configuration or menu needs to use these options.


Masked password prompts
-----------------------
The optional -password flag renders '*' instead of the characters in the
input field, while Return writes the actual input to standard output for
piping to a secure consumer. The password is never passed in argv by dmenu.
The caller must not log, echo or put it in shell command-line arguments.
Preview and password mode cannot be used at the same time.

Example (requires an X11 session):

    password=$(printf '' | dmenu -password -title 'Wi-Fi password' -p Password)

Never use the unmasked default dmenu input for secrets, and keep the resulting
variable in memory only as briefly as possible.
